{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I have complete context. Let me note:\n\n- task1 (my task): create `.rick/domain/spec.md` — the spec 规范 (template/规范), NOT rick-spec.md (that's task2 which creates `.rick/domain/rick-spec.md`).\n- task2 depends on task1 and will create `.rick/domain/rick-spec.md`.\n\nImportant: task1's spec.md is the规范 document. task2's rick-spec.md is the first actual spec.\n\nSo my spec.md needs:\n1. Define what spec is (结构化自然语言工程实现契约)\n2. Four-element structure template (模块边界/职责/接口契约/验收标准, each with 说明 + 占位示例)\n3. spec 与 domain 其他文档的关系\n4. Acceptance criteria: 功能等价 = 通过所有功能验收 (spec → 开发计划 → 功能等价实现); actionable criteria for \"丢弃源码 → AI 重构功能等价 rick\" (enumerate which commands dry-run/check/集成测试 must pass)\n5. 承载本次重构收敛结论 (rick = 引导程序, env 四职责, runtime 职责, handler 职责, 下沉策略)\n\nThe four elements placeholder examples should use the rick refactor conclusions as the example content, so the规范 \"承载\" the conclusions.\n\nNow let me look at what commands exist in the project for the \"可操作判据\" (actionable criteria). From commands.md and architecture.md:\n- `rick doing --dry-run` / `rick plan --dry-run` / `rick learning --dry-run` / `rick dream --dry-run` / `rick human-loop --dry-run` / `rick ctrl --dry-run`\n- `rick tools doing_check` / `plan_check` / `learning_check` / `dream_check`\n- `go test` (unit tests)\n- 集成测试 (bash integration tests)\n\nThe actionable criteria for \"丢弃源码 → AI 重构出功能等价 rick\" should list:\n- `go test ./...` 全量单测通过\n- `rick <cmd> --dry-run` for all commands (doing/plan/learning/easy/dream/ctrl/human-loop) outputs correct prompt (no `{{` leak)\n- `rick tools <check>` (plan_check/doing_check/learning_check/dream_check) all pass\n- 集成测试 (bash integration tests) pass\n\nLet me check the commands.md / project-conventions.md for the exact integration test commands. Let me also check what `easy` command does. Let me quickly grep.\n\nActually I have enough. Let me check project-conventions.md briefly to know build/test commands and integration tests."}}
