{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The doing_check:\n1. tasks.json exists and parseable ✓ (exists)\n2. debug/ dir: if no debug/ dir, return nil (fine). Currently no debug/ dir, so OK.\n3. No task in \"running\" zombie state — task1 is \"running\"! This is a problem.\n4. All \"success\" tasks have commit_hash.\n\nCurrently task1 status = \"running\" (from tasks.json). The check requires: no tasks in \"running\" state, and success tasks have commit_hash.\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Complete the task: set task1 status to \"success\" + commit_hash\n2. Commit the files\n\nLet me look at how the doing flow normally marks a task success. There's a \"mark-task-success\" skill. Let me read it.\n\nActually, the typical flow: the agent does the work, commits, then updates tasks.json to set status=\"success\" and commit_hash=<commit>, then runs doing_check.\n\nLet me read the mark-task-success skill and the tasks_json.go to understand the update mechanism."}}
